{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:67a1e1cbbe66b5a0","name":"Refitted Weapon Template","source":{"id":"source:reference-67a1e1cbbe66b5a0","title":"Refitted Weapon Template","revision":20287,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:34:08Z","sha256":"2e3ed17f7015ea57e022b2edcb1a6ab221b7e8fad7dec583573cdebe7fa59e3a","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20287","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Refitted%20Weapon%20Template&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-67a1e1cbbe66b5a0","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Legacy Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 20% credits more than the base item. All Refitted Weapons gain the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rare"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rare"}," availability, if they do not already have it.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Applicable To:"]}," Weapons (pre-Legacy Era; excluding ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]}," Weapons)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When a character ",{"tag":"a","children":["Refits"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Refits"}," a weapon, he or she upgrades its interchangeable parts with components that use the latest advances in weapon technology. Refitted Weapons have the following changes to their statistics:\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weapons:"]}," Since Refitted Weapons combine antiquated technology with modern components, sometimes the weapon must be treated gently and repairs can be challenging. A Refitted Weapon increases the base DC of any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check made to build or repair the weapon by +5. A Refitted Weapon can use standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["Energy Cells"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Energy_Cells"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Power Packs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Power_Packs"},". Additionally, weapons that use ",{"tag":"a","children":["Power Packs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Power_Packs"}," to provide ammunition have their number of shots that can be fired before the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Power Pack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Power_Pack","referenceId":"reference:2b783ab0537ca5d0"}," must be replaced increased by 10%.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Unlike normal weapons, Refitted Weapons require extra maintenance to ensure that they continue to function as expected. Once per week the weapon must receive regular maintenance, which requires 1 hour of work (no ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check required, though a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tool Kit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tool_Kit","referenceId":"reference:b833f332464890b5"}," is necessary to perform the maintenance). Failure to perform this maintenance move the weapon -1 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persistent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persistent"}," step down the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"}," for each day it does not receive maintenance after one week.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
